"text": "1984", "bbox": [1057, 1563, 1104, 1585], "src": "text"}], "refs": [], "referenced_by": [], "issues": [], "reading_order": "[title] Form {June 1983) 10-920 UNITED STATES NATIONAL DEPARTMENT PARK SERVICE OF THE INTERIOR\n10-920\nForm | UNITED | STATES | DEPARTMENT | OF | THE | INTERIOR\n{June | 1983) | NATIONAL | PARK | SERVICE\nARCHITECTURAL | DATA | FORM\nSTATE | COUNTY | TOWN | OR | VICINITY\nHawaii | Honolulu | Honolulu\nHISTORIC | NAME | OF | STRUCTURE | (INCLUDE | SOURCE | FOR | NAME) | HA8S | NO.\nlolani | Palace | Hl-1\nSECONDARY | OR | COMMON | NAMES | OF | STRUCTURE\nCOMPLETE | ADDRESS | (DESCRIBE | LOCATION | FOR | RURAL | SITES)\nKing | & | Richards | Streets | (in | center | of | \"Palace | Square,\" | bordered | by | King, | Richards, | Hotel,\nStreets').\nand | Punchbowl\nDATE | OF | CONSTRUCTION | (INCLUDE | SOURCE) | ARCHITECT(S) | (INCLUDESOURCE)\nDec. | 1879 | - | cornerstone | laid | Thos. | J. | Baker, | Charles | J. | Wall, | Isaac | Moore\nDec. | 1882 | - | complRt.*A\nSIGNIFICANCE | (ARCHITECTURAL | AND | HISTORICAL, | INCLUDE | ORIGINAL | USE | OF | STRUCTURE)\nResidence | of | the | last | two | royal | rulers | of | Hawaii. | Scene | of | transfer | of | government | to | the\nUnited | States | in | 1898. | From | 1898 | to | 1960s, | the | palace | served | as | the | capitol | of | Hawaii. | When\nbuilt, | the | palace | was | the | most | elaborate | structure | in | the | Hawaiian | Islands.\nSTYLE | (IF | APPROPRIATE)\nModified | Italianate/Second | Empire\nMATERIAL | OF | CONSTRUCTION | (INCLUDE | STRUCTURAL | SYSTEMS)\nBrick, | faced | with | cement. | Concrete | block | trim. | Cast-iron | columns | and | railings\nSHAPE | AND | DIMENSIONS | OF | STRUCTURE | (SKETCHED | FLOOR | PLANS | ON | SEPARATE | PAGES | ARE | ACCEPTABLE)\n(See | HABS | drawings). | Overall | dimensions | are | 139'-7\" | x | 99'-3\"\nEXTERIOR | FEATURES | OF | NOTE\nFour | corner | towers | with | mansard | roofs; | two | taller | central | towers | on | long | facades; | two-tierbd\ncast-iron | porticoes | (lanais) | between | towers | on | all | sides; | elaborate | decorative | trim, | includ-\ning | quoins, | bracketed | cornices, | window | frames.\nINTERIOR | FEATURES | OF | NOTE | (DESCRIBE | FLOOR | PLANS, | IF | NOT | SKETCHED)\nFree-standing | grand | stairway; | throne | room. | Extensive | use | of | rare | woods. | Etched | glass\npanels | in | doors | contain | representations | of | Hawaiian | flora | and | fauna. | Elaborate | plaster\ncornices | and | ceilings.\nMAJOR | ALTERATIONS | AND | ADDITIONS | WITH | DATES\n1929-30: | steel | and | reinforced | concrete | framing | replaced | original | wooden | framing. | Restore\nafter | capitol | moved | to | new | building | in | 1970s, | A | complete | list | of | alterations | may | be | found\non | pages | 102-103 | of | George | Moore | j3t. | al.: | lolani | Palace | Restoration | (Honolulu, | 1970)\nPRESENT | CONDITION | AND | USE\nMuseum, | in | excellent | condition\n^\nOTHER | INFORMATION | AS | APPROPRIATE | See | fleld | records | accompanylng | thlfJ | report | for | reprint\nof | several | articles | giving | additional | architectural | and | historical | information.\nSOURCES | OF | INFORMATION | (INCLUDING | LISTING | ON | NATIONAL | REGISTER, | STATE | REGISTERS, | ETC.)\nlolani | Palace | is | a | National | Historic | Landmark. | See | \"Major | Alterations | and | Additions | with\nDates\" | above | for | a | major | bibliographic | reference; | also | see | HABS | field | records | accompanying\nthis | report.\nCOMPILER, | AFFILIATION | DATE\nS. | A. | Chambers, | Jr., | Architectural | Historian, | HABS\nNov. | 1984"}